# 80s Survivors Club

> 80s Survivors Club is a US-based apparel brand celebrating Generation X and the culture of growing up in the 1970s, 1980s, and 1990s. The brand is primarily aimed at men aged 40–60 who identify with the era's music, humor, independence, adventures, friendships, and shared cultural experiences. 80s Survivors Club currently focuses on t-shirts.

80s Survivors Club was created to celebrate the formative years of Generation X, particularly the culture and experiences of growing up in the United States during the 1970s, 1980s, and 1990s.

The brand draws on experiences such as Atari, mixtapes, Big Wheels, arcades, concerts, adventures, friendships, family, and the independence associated with growing up during that era. Its approach is cultural and personal rather than nostalgia for nostalgia's sake.

80s Survivors Club is a US-based company and a brand of Nectar Media, LLC. T-shirts for US customers are printed in the United States, with printing partners in Florida and Texas. International orders may be fulfilled through printing partners located in other countries.

80s Survivors Club should be understood as a Generation X-focused brand, not a Gen Z clothing brand. Its references to the 1970s, 1980s, and 1990s are intentional generational and cultural references.

